<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopoldo O'Donnell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1867">1867</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopoldo O'Donnell was a Spanish general and politician of Irish descent who led the Liberal Union and served three times as prime minister between 1856 and 1866. His long government of 1858 to 1863 waged the Hispano-Moroccan War of 1859–1860, for which he was made Duke of Tetuan, and accepted the reannexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> in 1861. It also sent Spanish forces to join the intervention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopoldo-odonnell.jpg" alt="Leopoldo O'Donnell" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raimundo de Madrazo y Garreta · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madrazo,_Raimundo_de_(Leopoldo_O%27Donnell).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
